        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209-a9">

                <pb facs="0345" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg303"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 30, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to transmit copies of
                    a letter from the consul of the United States at Liverpool, and of two more
                    depositions relating to the case of the Phantom. I do not presume that they will
                    have any effect in varying the reply already given to my former representations
                    in your lordship’s note of the 27th instant. Notwithstanding the report made
                    concerning the objects of that vessel, I greatly fear that she will turn up in
                    America, much in the character of the Georgiana. I can only hope for the sake of
                    the harmony of both countries that she may meet with the same fate.</p>
                <p>I pray, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>










